WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.800
Azure AI.

2
00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:05.085
OpenAI models wrapped in enterprise controls.

3
00:00:05.085 --> 00:00:07.008
The controls are the product.

4
00:00:07.008 --> 00:00:08.533
Let's see how it works.

5
00:00:09.733 --> 00:00:15.067
Azure OpenAI Service is OpenAI models wrapped in enterprise controls.

6
00:00:15.367 --> 00:00:17.279
First, regional data residency.

7
00:00:17.279 --> 00:00:21.167
Prompts and completions are processed in the region you choose.

8
00:00:21.467 --> 00:00:24.033
Second, content filters you can configure.

9
00:00:24.333 --> 00:00:25.933
Third, private networking.

10
00:00:26.233 --> 00:00:31.000
And Microsoft grade compliance paperwork that procurement departments already trust.

11
00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:34.567
Here is the telling difference in the API.

12
00:00:34.867 --> 00:00:36.233
You don't call a model name.

13
00:00:36.533 --> 00:00:38.200
You call your own deployment name.

14
00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:40.533
Follow a request.

15
00:00:40.833 --> 00:00:43.000
Your code targets the deployment name.

16
00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:47.667
The deployment pins a specific model version, with the capacity you chose.

17
00:00:47.967 --> 00:00:50.400
Your content filter policy is applied.

18
00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:53.567
And processing stays inside your chosen region.

19
00:00:54.767 --> 00:00:55.800
Here is the code.

20
00:00:56.100 --> 00:01:01.200
The client points at your own Azure resource endpoint, with a key and an API version.

21
00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:05.767
Then in the model field, we put our deployment name, not the vendor's model name.

22
00:01:06.067 --> 00:01:10.500
The deployment pins the version, region, capacity, and filter policy.

23
00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:13.833
Here's the meeting that shows the value.

24
00:01:14.133 --> 00:01:22.100
A bank loves your ticket triage demo, but compliance has one non-negotiable line: customer data must not leave India.

25
00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:25.167
The public OpenAI API is a no.

26
00:01:25.467 --> 00:01:32.347
Azure OpenAI with a deployment in Central India is a yes, with the filter policy and audit trail attached.

27
00:01:32.347 --> 00:01:34.100
Your prompts didn't change.

28
00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:36.567
The deployment made the deal signable.

29
00:01:37.767 --> 00:01:38.710
Let's recap.

30
00:01:38.710 --> 00:01:43.033
Azure OpenAI is OpenAI models plus enterprise controls.

31
00:01:43.333 --> 00:01:46.567
That means residency, filters, and private networking.

32
00:01:46.867 --> 00:01:49.400
You call your deployment name, not the model name.

33
00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:54.633
And that deployment is your pinned, governed instance, not the vendor's moving target.
